KiCad Track Gloss
=================

This standalone plugin derives its octolinear track-chain smoothing approach
from KiCadRoutingTools by DrAndyHaas:

    https://github.com/drandyhaas/KiCadRoutingTools

Derived material includes the chain recognition, 0/45/90-degree shortcut
search, improvement gate, obstacle checks, and connectivity-preservation
strategy originally implemented in py_router/pcb_modification.py in
smooth_octolinear_chains().

The standalone adaptation in the fca1 KiCadRoutingTools fork adds explicit
selected-track KIID scoping, UUID-less geometric fallback keys, an API-neutral
engine, SWIG board adaptation, temporary-copy native KiCad DRC comparison,
preview/settings UI, rollback, independent branding, and PCM packaging.

The original MIT license and copyright notice are preserved in LICENSE.
Nothing in this adaptation presents the derived smoothing algorithm as an
entirely new invention.

